---
/** Privacy policy: hosting logs, no cookies or third parties, the theme preference (issue #33). */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { email, legalName, mailtoHref } from '../lib/contact';

// Link GitHub's own wording rather than paraphrasing it (issue #33).
// Update this page when hosting moves to AWS (Phase 2) or analytics are added (Phase 4).
const pagesDataUrl =
  'https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/about-github-pages#data-collection';
const githubPrivacyUrl =
  'https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy · Medhini Oak"
  description="PLACEHOLDER: one-sentence description of the privacy page"
>
  <div class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>
      This site has no cookies, no analytics, no embeds and no tracking. This
      page explains the little data that is processed when you visit it.
    </p>

    <section aria-labelledby="responsible-title">
      <h2 id="responsible-title">Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>{legalName}</p>
      <p>
        Email: <a href={mailtoHref(email)}>{email}</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        More details are in the <a href="/impressum/">Impressum</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="hosting-title">
      <h2 id="hosting-title">Hosting and server logs</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc. in the
        USA. When you open a page, your browser sends a request to GitHub's
        servers, and GitHub processes your IP address to deliver the page.
        According to GitHub, the IP address of every visitor is logged and
        stored for security purposes. I have no access to these logs.
      </p>
      <p>
        GitHub describes this in its documentation on{' '}
        <a href={pagesDataUrl}>data collection for GitHub Pages</a> and in the{' '}
        <a href={githubPrivacyUrl}>GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="basis-title">
      <h2 id="basis-title">Legal basis and retention</h2>
      <p>
        The processing is based on legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR):
        delivering the site securely and reliably.
      </p>
      <p>
        GitHub does not publish a specific retention period for these logs. Its
        privacy statement says that retention depends on the purpose and on
        legal obligations; see the links above.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="third-title">
      <h2 id="third-title">No cookies, analytics or third parties</h2>
      <p>
        The site sets no cookies and uses no analytics, trackers or embedded
        content. All fonts, scripts and images come from this site itself; your
        browser makes no requests to anyone else.
      </p>
      <p>
        Links to other services, such as GitHub, LinkedIn, YouTube or Twitch,
        are plain links. Those services only receive data from you if you follow
        a link, and then their own privacy policies apply.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="email-title">
      <h2 id="email-title">Email</h2>
      <p>
        The "Email me" button is a <code>mailto:</code> link. It opens your own
        mail app; the site itself receives and stores nothing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="theme-title">
      <h2 id="theme-title">Your theme preference</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing is stored until you use the theme toggle. If you choose light or
        dark, that choice is saved in your browser's local storage under the key{' '}
        <code>theme</code>, so the site remembers it on your next visit. It
        stays in your browser and is never sent anywhere.
      </p>
      <p>
        To remove it, choose "system" with the toggle, or clear this site's data
        in your browser settings.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="rights-title">
      <h2 id="rights-title">Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>access the personal data held about you (Art. 15)</li>
        <li>have it corrected (Art. 16)</li>
        <li>have it erased (Art. 17)</li>
        <li>have its processing restricted (Art. 18)</li>
        <li>object to its processing (Art. 21)</li>
        <li>
          lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority, in
          particular in the EU member state where you live or work, or where you
          believe your data was misused (Art. 77)
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To use these rights, email me at <a href={mailtoHref(email)}>{email}</a>
        . For the server logs, you can also contact GitHub directly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="changes-title">
      <h2 id="changes-title">Changes</h2>
      <p>
        This policy is updated whenever the site changes how it handles data,
        for example when it moves to a different host.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal,
  .legal section {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: start;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .legal section {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
  }

  .legal ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
</style>
